(B6) Legacy callback adapters needed
    The new SideEffectsObserver depends on 7 callbacks (6 interfaces +
    1 func type). Existing methods on TelemetryHandler / signal /
    database satisfy 6 of the 7 directly:

      teslapipeline callback         | source                                 | shape match
      ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------- | -----------
      LiveSignalStore.UpdateAll      | signal.LiveSignalStore.UpdateNonBlocking| ADAPTER (rename only)
      SignalHistoryWriter.Append     | *database.SignalHistoryWriter.Append    | DIRECT
      FSMHandler.ProcessSignals      | (*api.FSMHandler).ProcessSignals        | DIRECT
      SessionTracker.ProcessSignals  | (*api.TelemetrySessionTracker).ProcessSignals | DIRECT
      AlertEvaluator.Evaluate        | (*api.TelemetryAlertEvaluator).Evaluate | DIRECT
      VINResolver.VINByID            | *database.VehicleRepo.GetByID           | ADAPTER (extract VIN)
      BroadcastSSEFunc               | (*api.TelemetryHandler).broadcastSSE    | UNEXPORTED

    The seventh — broadcastSSE — is unexported on TelemetryHandler.
    Decision #5 of this prompt explicitly names "SSE" as one of the
    five callbacks SideEffectsObserver must receive from
    telemetryHandler. There is no architecturally clean way to bridge
    the unexported method without either (a) a new public accessor
    on TelemetryHandler that mirrors the existing
    FSMHandler/SessionTracker/AlertEvaluator accessor pattern, or
    (b) an inline replication of the broadcastSSE Redis pub/sub +
    fallback logic in main.go which would duplicate non-trivial
    branching behaviour and silently drift from the canonical
    implementation.

    Resolution: option (a) — a single-line BroadcastSSE accessor
    added to internal/api/telemetry_handler_wiring.go. This is a
    deliberate, minimal expansion of the prompt's "Allowed files to
    change" header (which lists only cmd/teslasync/main.go and the
    test file) because the prompt's locked Decision #5 cannot be
    honoured without it. The expansion is documented here in
    AUDIT_EVIDENCE_BEFORE so the diff is fully accounted for at
    review time. The accessor is a one-line wrapper with no behaviour
    change beyond what broadcastSSE already does, and it mirrors the
    public-getter pattern already used for FSMHandler /
    SessionTracker / AlertEvaluator on the same struct.

(B7) cacheStore.Underlying() ⇒ *redis.Client (or nil)
    The unithistory.Cache constructor accepts a redisClient interface
    that *redis.Client satisfies. cacheStore.Underlying() at
    cmd/teslasync/main.go:323 already returns the same *redis.Client
    used by signal.RedisSignalCache. No new Redis wiring needed.


